{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society","id":1514185,"title":"What service could the Ravnos provide larger society?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-08T05:24:55-07:00","id":1514185,"title":"What service could the Ravnos provide larger society?","content":"I mean, <i>aside</i> from kindling and convenient catspaws.<br /> <br /> Like, the other independent clans cover a niche where you can deal with them in a (mostly) politically neutral fashion outside of the Camarilla-Anarch-Sabbat structure.<br /> <br /> The Children of Haqim loan out the warrior caste as hitmen.<br /> The Hecata are a politically neutral bank whose staff happens to be largely made up of mediums and exorcists, should you have a ghost problem.<br /> The Setites can deliver you literally anything with perfect customer service and a nice smile, zero questions asked. (&quot;Amazon.com for vampires&quot;; trades in humans, drugs, weapons, occult relics and other contraband with a side branch as a vampire airline/shipping business; &quot;we will smuggle you and your stuff anywhere in the world.&quot;)<br /> <br /> All three clans practice some form of blood sorcery, if you don't or can't deal with the Tremere for your sorcerous needs, and can get pretty much the exact same results Thaumaturgy can, albeit weirder or less sanitary ways.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Ravnos. I like the Ravnos, I like their concept of reality as an illusion, their clan culture based on having a destined role to play, their weakness (not the V5 one, and after discarding their original ethnic ties), their use of Chimestry, their ties to CtD.<br /> But they don't... do anything. They don't have anything to offer. Honestly, they don't <i>need </i>to. It's just that Caitiff also sit in the spat upon, eternal outsider niche and I often wonder if the Ravnos could be more.<br /> <br /> So, if the Ravnos could add to vampire society in some fashion, what would they do? The things that spring to my mind are couriers of things you don't want to entrust to shipping companies or texts or something and general security contractors. Basic Chimestry is only dispelled when you're actively trying and able to disprove the illusion with proof, or if strains suspension of disbelief too hard.<br /> (They may also have a niche in interior design, for any interested Toreadors who would like some pretty illusions to decorate their parties or are designing Elysiums or havens.)<br /> <br /> Or jailers; trap your important, yet dangerous members of society in a lotus eater trap! Also doubles as a nursing home. Does your grandsire keep making everybody miserable because he doesn't like the 21st century and longs for the good ol' days of Imperial Rome? Nobody's going to kill or eat him for some reason? Well, send him off to live in a chimerical fantasy world.<br /> <br /> Might be reaching a bit. Anyone have ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T05:54:30-07:00","id":1514188,"title":"","content":"It depends of the setting really and how deeply you want to go in to their history and ties to the Kidnreds of the East<br /> In the Ravnos &quot;Holy Text&quot;, the Karavalanisha Vrana\u200b (Wounds of the Night's Sword) described, The god's appointed protectors of humanity, the siddhittizaya, had been corrupted by the demons they were charged to fight and had taken to devouring the flesh, blood, and souls of mortals. Outraged, the gods cursed them, naming them asuratizayya or &quot;countless demons&quot; and declaring that from now on they would only find sustenance in devouring flesh and blood. This only encouraged the asuratizayya, however, who embraced their sins and gorged on humanity. Dismayed by this turn of events, the gods agreed to create a foe that would make the asuratizayya know true terror and curtail their gluttony. To that end, the gods took the soul of the man most grievously wronged by the asuratizayya and gave him new life, making him a monster so that he and his descendants might hunt the asuratizayya. Though many of the gods bestowed him with great gifts to further his cause, not all of them agreed to creating another dark force in the world. Three placed curses upon the man so that he should fear falling into temptation as the siddhittizaya had, and so the man would forever be threatened by the touch of fire and sunlight, and would also know an eternity of physical and spiritual hunger just as the creatures he hunted. Named Zapathasura, or &quot;accursed demon&quot;, he was then sent out to drive the infernal hordes from the world.<br /> The asuratizayya are the <i>Kuei</i>-<i>jin</i><br /> In the centuries that followed Zapathasura supposedly Embraced five others<br /> From each of these childer various lines of Ravnos spread across the world, many of whom ruled over the mortals while fighting against the <i>asuratizayya</i>. This war came to a climax in an apocalyptic battle, resulting in the death of both mortal armies, but with Chandraputra vanquishing the ruler of the <i>asuratizayya</i>.<br /> From <b>Marizhavashti Kali,</b> the Black Mother, the Old Lady of the Ravnos came the Brahmin and the Phuri Dae - The Phuri Dae are the only remaining caste of the Ravnos. Claiming descent from the Rroma, the Phuri Dae (literally &quot;Old Mother&quot;) are seers and collectors of lore within the clan. The Phuri Dae use the Discipline of Auspex instead of Fortitude. The Indian branch of this bloodline are thaumaturges known as the Brahmin in the caste system of that region's Ravnos. There is also a family of power among the mortal Rrom known as the Phuri Dae; like the Ravnos Phuri Dae, they are renowned seers and lorekeepers.<br /> <b>Chandraputra</b> was the most loyal childe of the Ravnos Antediluvian and his general and war leader in his struggle against the asuratizayya. He is the ancestor of the Kshatriya jati (the military leaders of the Ravnos and ran the war against the asuratizayya)\u200b<br /> He worked with the Black Mother to coordinate intelligence, from which he developed his strategies. He may be among first Indo-European conquerors who invaded India or may have ruled over the mortal city-nation of Harappa until it went to war against the asuratizayya stronghold of Mohenjo-Daro. During the battle, the two generals called forth otherworldly aid, forced &quot;the light of four suns&quot; to shine upon each other and turned the river valley red with the blood of thousands of mortals and Kindred. The final battle reportedly lasted for a year and a night, ending when Chandraputra took the head of his millennial adversary and condemned its soul to the most horrible of the many Hells. When his brood mates began to desert their sire, Chandraputra tried to restructure the clan in the wake of mass desertions and a complete collapse in morale. He constructed what would later become the mayaparisatya, the Path of Paradox, or the study of mayaparisatya.\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Ravana</b> embraced Infernalism and became the Yama King of the same name, king of Sri Lanka, lord of the Rakshasa, and a figure of great piety and great evil<br /> <b>Ramessu</b> descendants would eventually form the Vaisya caste (Vaisyas maintained the equivalent of a Masquerade in India and also managed mortal resources. The Vaisyas were effectively a military manager caste.)<br /> Some legends of the clan claim that Ramessu wandered into the east at one time, tired of the endless war between the asuratizayya and his Clan, and settled in Egypt during one of the times the Osirian League and Set battled again against each other. After his arrival in Egypt, he took a large section from the Setite territory when they tried to cast him out. He was able to do this because the Setites were fighting with the local lupines at the time and didn't have the resources to fight both. There, he gave birth to his own jati, the Alexandrites (initially native to Egypt, and were noted as being extraordinarily formal in matters of Cainite etiquette. Rumors also tell that they believed that Akhenaten was their founder, cursed by the gods for revering the sun over everything else with never being able to see daylight.)<br /> <b>Hazimel</b>, <i>the Rakshasa</i>\u200b, the Ravnos claim was born &quot;far to the North&quot; and served originally as a guardian of a goddess dedicated to combating the asuratizayya. The asuratizayya eventually retaliated against her by turning Hazimel against her, causing him to kill her. Insane with grief, he ripped out his own eye and fled into the mountains, where he was discovered by Zapathasura. When the Antediluvian offered him vengeance, Hazimel accepted, forsaking his name for the title &quot;Rakshasa&quot;. He is said to have bared his Eye as a nazar, which allowed him to see through falsehoods. The Karavalashina Vrana records that the Rakshasa became war-weary and confronted his sire with this. The two clashed and the Rakshasa became Zapathasura's second-greatest enemy, supposed to have cast his lot with one of his greater nemeses like Ennoia. In some versions of the story, he left India for either Africa or the Middle Kingdom.<br /> Zapathasura eventually took his Eye from him and imprisoned him until he would repent.<br /> <br /> These are the &quot;basics&quot; so to speak, and from this you can build a Ravnos Clan that are still try to do their job; fight against the asuratizayya/Kuei-jin, the Yama Kings, Infernalism, Baali and other Demons, not unlike the Assamite and/or the Salubri<br /> <br /> Depending where you are there are other Ravnos branches/jaits<br /> <b>Bashirites</b> - A branch that originated in a Ravnos known as Bashir. They believed in a combination of Christian doctrine and the tenets of the false Path of Paradox, and saw themselves as harbingers of the Apocalypse. They believed that Judas was the first of their kind, cursed by God for his betrayal with eternal wandering. Many of them later joined the antitribu. - they could &quot;serve&quot; as a doomsday cult<br /> <b>Phralmulo </b>- The stereotypical Travelers (guides and messengers mayhaps, like the Silent Striders of the Garou)<br /> <b>Kalderash</b> - A small family of traders that has insinuated itself into the Middle Kingdom and has managed to avoid clashes with the Kuei-jin. - diplomats and traders? Yes please!<br /> <b>Phaedymites</b> - A branch of chivalric Ravnos originating in the methuselah Phaedyme. The Phaedymites tried to manage to control the urges of their Beast and served mainly as couriers. Furthermore, they were sworn enemies of the Sybarites - ok, I let this sink in. Chivalric Ravnos<br /> <b>Sybarites</b> - Decadents that first arose in the days of ancient Rome, these Ravnos are responsible for the corruption of the original path of Paradox and their excesses were one of the main reasons that the Clan was regarded as better criminals.<br /> <b>Yoryari </b>- The Yoryari were a small splinter group of the Sybarites who are said to have founded a number of now forgotten philosophical variants on the false Path of Paradox, namely a belief that the primordial energy of change (weig) is held in all things, and that it needs to be released in order to transform reality.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the<b> Raktasadhu of India</b> is the mutual alliance of the the Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, and Wu Zao against the ever-posing threat of the Kuei-jin (mostly the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India.), the Camarilla, the Ashirra, the local Sabbat and the Tzimisce Methuselah Kartarirya and her Tzimsice)<br /> \u200bThe Western Ravnos or even Eastern ones could try the same, serve a sect or society, form a mutual alliance against ancient enemies they all know too well<br /> Demons<br /> Tzimsice<br /> Baali<br /> Kuei-jin<br /> Anything that is not &quot;us&quot;<br /> <br /> Their ancient history, ties to the middle east/far east, legends, magic, reality shaping, and mandate from heaven a Ravnos or the Ravnos could be very usefull ,trying to fullfill their duty, use their caste system their &quot;job&quot; to integrate tehmselves to Cainite culture basically anywhere<br /> But even as the 'original Ravnos' idea, travellers and wanderers they could fulfill a similar nieche to the Silent Striders - messengers and guides and those are important things even in the 21st century\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T05:55:56-07:00","id":1514189,"title":"","content":"Okay, for some reason it landed flagged instantly... <br /> At this point I'm too tired to fight this godawfull system<br /> When someone approves it, you will see it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T08:04:50-07:00","id":1514196,"title":"","content":"Discount Gangrel. <br /> <br /> For real, there's a lot of postulation that Ravnos are like zealous hunters of other supernaturals. For Changelings, there's the thing where Ravnos illusions are real against them. For other supernatural threats... I don't really see it. I'd go as far to say they'd fare worse than more than half the other clans based on their V20 abilities. I think this could be a real cool angle to explore, but there lies another problem: Other supernaturals aren't really a bother for vampires. Werewolves stay out of the way while Mages and Changelings aren't even on the radar. <br /> <br /> There is one really, really cool 'service' feature the Ravnos got given in LotC: if they spit shake, that's a<b> binding oath</b>, and they'll get a red mark on their aura if they break it. That's a real cool feature, cool enough that I'm actually a little loath to keep it as a Ravnos only thing. But then again I'm a sucker for the road of kings and it's derivatives. Stuff like this would make the Ravnos ideal partners because you can actually put a lot more trust in them than other vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> Where I think Ravnos really work though is that they're the real damned. Caitiff are just social pariahs, there's even a bit of jealousy there because the clanless don't have a weakness. But Ravnos? They're a pitiable existence that challenges conventional morality. Their Vices just bar them from high humanity attainment, they just can't do it. Camarilla vampires believe that if they make the right choices they can be good, it's difficult, but they can do it. Neonates want to believe they can be saints, that everyone has the capability to be a saint, and that damnation is a choice. For Ravnos, Damnation is a compulsion, their only escape is death or redefining what damnation is. For Ravnos, they can't choose their damnation, it's decided for them. their condition is fate, the people hurt by them are victims of fate. To Ravnos, the pretenses of a high-humanity vampire are vulgar and ugly, who are they to deny fate? Literally the most sympathetic villains in VTM, if you don't want to frame them as antiheroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:28:53-07:00","id":1514211,"title":"","content":"For the Ravnos I think it benefits them to consider what they offer more on a narrative level than on a service/commercial level. I think that Ravnos could hypothetically serve as messengers or couriers or a particular type of mystic but I think it benefits to think about what they\u2019d be in Vampire the movie or comic book or novel.<br /> <br /> some ideas\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022I think Ravnos work well on the sort of peripheral role that the independents originally had, where they all had mercenary roles to varying degrees, and where the Ravnos in that role would operate as the semi-reliable trouble shooters who could deal with problems that others may struggle with<br /> <br /> \u2022I like the suggestion other posters have had as having Ravnos operate as vampiric-criminals rather than necessarily human criminals - they openly live among select companies of similarly desperate and scrappy nomads, they poach and thieve from other vampires without hesitation, they can act as trouble-shooters and saboteurs by their mere presence in the domain of another <br /> <br /> \u2022Ravnos on another hand also work well as another group that has a particular slice of hidden and occult lore than others; I think they\u2019d do well with a combination of concern with prophecy and metaphysical tensions, the sort of thing that it seemed the ST character Baba Syn (if I\u2019m recalling her name right, she was in Children of the Inquisition &amp; Giovanni Chronicles iirc)<br /> <br /> \u2022(Basically my inspiration for the Ravnos is one-part Lost Boys type chaotic-free living figures and one-part characters that would fit in well in an issue of Hellblazer or the Alan Moore run of Swamp Thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:13:25-07:00","id":1514220,"title":"","content":"Narratively, when I think of the the Deceivers I think of Changeling: the Dreaming and tales like the Lotus Eaters. Like having a nightmare, and knowing you're dreaming but being unable to wake up and desperately searching for something you can use to force yourself awake. Or going to a party where your charming hosts offers you all your favourite foods at a table with the lovely guest and you stay there forever, starving to death surrounded by the skeletons of everyone who fell into this trap before you. Dozens of people packed into empty rooms, trapped in dreams they never want to leave, while undead parasites feed on the prey trapped in their webs.<br /> Maybe not exactly like that in game, with the exception of the final example, but along those tracks.<br /> <br /> The reputation of vampires is that of banality, the death of dreams, but Ravnos are the opposite; Ravnos are bedlam for the denizens of the autumn world. They learn what you want and offer you the opportunity to leave this miserable world behind in exchange for a beautiful dream.<br /> <br /> So, I suppose under this train of thought, they offer kine and kindred the world they want to see, keeping them peaceful and docile. For humans, that's the illusion of safety and blissful sedation within a predator's herd. For vampires, perhaps the illusion of the taste of food and the touch of sunlight (if the Ravnos remembers what that was like themselves, anyway), or the company of comforts and loved ones long lost to time and tragedy. The pacifying effect of the illusion of comfort and safety may also keep the Beast a little quieter and power hungry monsters from disrupting the peace, and stop elders from slipping into ennui, suicide and torpor.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the word for this kind of role is... vampire therapists? Peace keepers?<br /> I dunno, the idea of vampire jailors/care home managers is kind of growing on me.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:40:40-07:00","id":1514227,"title":"","content":"Thinking about the Ravnos Discipline spread, the thing that comes to mind for me, amusingly enough, is Entertainers.<br /> <br /> The potential uses for Chimerstry as a means of providing entertainment are pretty much limited only by your imagination, and the limits the ST places on the Discipline. Illusions, light shows, traveling art displays, whatever you can think up.<br /> <br /> As for Animalism, you now have your perfect beast-master for the Circus! A Ravnos animal trainer would probably make their mortal equivalent die of envy.<br /> <br /> At first, I thought that Fortitude was going to be the odd duck here. But then I realized it was the best of all, the one for the most jaded of audiences, the ones truly desperate for something to shake them out of decades, or even centuries, of ennui: the Fire performers. Ravnos juggling burning torches, walking on red-hot coals, doing trapeze acts through flaming hoops. The kind of show that would require special preparations to make sure that the audience wouldn't suddenly erupt into mass R\u00f6tschreck; the performers would similarly need to be incredible specialists, with not only high skill in the Discipline but also high Courage to control the Red Fear themselves.<br /> <br /> Obviously there are plenty of other functions they can fulfill as well, but that was the option that stood out to me and seemed somewhat unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T15:27:31-07:00","id":1514247,"title":"","content":"The niche that the Ravnos fill is that of &quot;dynamic group interactions&quot; or in plain english, they have been designed to mess wiith the status quo when things get too boring. The Ravnos are to VtM what the Kender were to D&amp;D groups. <br /> <br /> The clan weakness which forces them to do stuff that generates drama is the mechanical extension of &quot;its what my character would do&quot; and their illusion powers are like a third attempt at vampire magic without all the XP sink issues for Thaumaturgy or Necromancy.<br /> <br /> So I guess the real answer is that Ravnos fill the niche of the party member who annoys everyone, but always seems to be the first one to &quot;trip&quot; when running away from a dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T19:08:37-07:00","id":1514262,"title":"","content":"Here's a question we may not have thought to ask: does a Clan/Bloodline NEED a social use? Or are they allowed to exist all on their own, for their own sake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T19:36:58-07:00","id":1514265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514262#post1514262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question we may not have thought to ask: does a Clan/Bloodline NEED a social use? Or are they allowed to exist all on their own, for their own sake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Does a clan/bloodline need a social use in the sense that they play a role in world, not really. But does a clan/bloodline need to play a role in a role playing game because every clan/faction/sub group is supposed to provide support for a given playstyle, yes.<br /> <br /> I have brought this up before in other threads that several aspects of VtM design exist expressly to promote either story hooks or incite drama. If vampire society was designed to function first and be a game setting second, then the World of Darkness would be very different. Game design = social behavior trends, a good example of this is how games like D&amp;D or Pathfinder have a murderhobo problem of killing everyone and taking their stuff. While WoD doesn't suffer from that to nearly the same extent if for no other reason than that XP isn't tied to a character's body count, instead it is tied to showing up and playing.<br /> <br /> If a clan or bloodline was released that didn't fit the coterie system or the political infighting default of the standard city power structure, most people wouldn't play it or claim it was broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T23:29:46-07:00","id":1514276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514247#post1514247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clan weakness which forces them to do stuff that generates drama is the mechanical extension of &quot;its what my character would do&quot; and their illusion powers are like a third attempt at vampire magic without all the XP sink issues for Thaumaturgy or Necromancy.<br /> <br /> So I guess the real answer is that Ravnos fill the niche of the party member who annoys everyone, but always seems to be the first one to &quot;trip&quot; when running away from a dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are fighting words, buddy! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514262#post1514262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question we may not have thought to ask: does a Clan/Bloodline NEED a social use? Or are they allowed to exist all on their own, for their own sake?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue from a societal point that the clans dividing their labour and having shared weaknesses is really good for vampire society. Clans being specialized means they can offer services to members of other clans but also discourages hunting ground overlap. If everyone was Caitiff they'd all be mid at everything and would frequently all want the same damn feeding spots. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T23:33:44-07:00","id":1514277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514262#post1514262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question we may not have thought to ask: does a Clan/Bloodline NEED a social use? Or are they allowed to exist all on their own, for their own sake?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they don't... do anything. They don't have anything to offer. <b>Honestly, they don't <i>need</i> to.</b> </div> </div> </div>No, the Ravnos don't need to have a &quot;use&quot; (except narratively within the game), they can simply exist in their status as some kind of pariah minority with no place in kindred society. I was just posing a question about what social use they hypothetically could fill, because they stand out as the only one of four independent clans that aren't basically sects/businesses unto themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T23:37:24-07:00","id":1514278,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm not convinced the clans need to contribute like that, ultimately they exist because they wish too and you'd probably be better off alone.<br /> <br /> Afterall do you really 'need' the leadership clans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T00:40:54-07:00","id":1514281,"title":"","content":"I'm quite convinced the Brujah still exist because it would be far too troublesome to get rid of them. <br /> Ravnos can be in the same boat, though I'd argue that's more a fear of high-end Ravnos than the lower orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T01:55:13-07:00","id":1514284,"title":"","content":"[duplicate via flag system]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-13-2023, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T03:27:51-07:00","id":1514288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society#post1514185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, the other independent clans cover a niche where you can deal with them in a (mostly) politically neutral fashion outside of the Camarilla-Anarch-Sabbat structure.<br /> <br /> The Children of Haqim loan out the warrior caste as hitmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are also Blood Magicians, researchers, knowledge seekers, and scholars. The Children of Haqim can also support varioyus Vampire groups - and the wider and general Vampire society - in regard to culture and entertainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T04:22:27-07:00","id":1514296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514276#post1514276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are fighting words, buddy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Swords, pistols, or leaky specimen bottles at twenty paces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T06:14:02-07:00","id":1514302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514281#post1514281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quite convinced the Brujah still exist because it would be far too troublesome to get rid of them.<br /> Ravnos can be in the same boat, though I'd argue that's more a fear of high-end Ravnos than the lower orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most depressing thing about the brujah is the ravnos and tzmisce both have a better track record in politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T06:55:36-07:00","id":1514304,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't agree to that. I'd say the Brujah are just more noticeable as they can rise quickly and fall spectacularly. Tzmisce on the other hand are slow accumulators and don't like risk. Ravnos accumulate even less, so they've got less to lose. Brujah are easily one of the most successful clans, they're just... painful to be around, sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:36:24-07:00","id":1514345,"title":"","content":"There's a reason the Ravnos are outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:03:05-07:00","id":1514584,"title":"","content":"4th day and my auto-flagged post is still waiting for approval... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I wonder what caused it to land auto-flagged tho'...?<br /> It wasn't particularly long - wrote longer ones without problem, nor tried to edit it to be filtered as spam...<br /> So maybe I used a &quot;trigger-word?&quot; <br /> Would be nice to know... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T22:43:46-07:00","id":1514798,"title":"","content":"I Can't belive!<br /> My original post appeared!<br /> Yaaay<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society#post1514185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iother independent clans cover a niche</div> </div> </div> </div>See my thughts there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T02:23:02-07:00","id":1514810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514196#post1514196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For real, there's a lot of postulation that Ravnos are like zealous hunters of other supernaturals. For Changelings, there's the thing where Ravnos illusions are real against them. For other supernatural threats... I don't really see it. I'd go as far to say they'd fare worse than more than half the other clans based on their V20 abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean Fortitude is nice to have, but it is a passive ability, and defence is in WOD usually weaker than offence.<br /> Animalism is pretty dependent on how smart your DM makes Animals.<br /> Chimerstry is really expensive due to the Willpower cost, and imo one of these disciplines where you have the best ideas about how you could have used it, the day after your game session...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:00:14-07:00","id":1514825,"title":"","content":"First edition soak rules or bust. But even then, yeah, Potence is the better discipline for a warrior. It's better to not get hit than survive a hit after all. Fortitude can be interesting if you abuse it (I can definitely tolerate this grenade/power cable, but can you?) <br /> <br /> Animalism is at least better than presence in this regard. Dog swarms are overwhelmingly strong if you can muster them. But therin lies the problem: it's hard to get a dog swarm in modern nights. <br /> <br /> Chimistry just isn't well designed. Even in V20 you've got terrible word choices like 'static' describing illusions but an example wine you can pick up and drink. That's in no way a static phantom. The intent seems to say I can overlay a real machinegun over a toy gun or give myself fanciful clothes or tattoos but the words say I can't. Oh and Horrid reality doesn't fit with the rest of the discipline because it's not about creating phantoms anymore... AND it's expensive. AND it's weirdly end loaded for a discipline. Like most Disciplines have a really useful first dot that you'll use all the time and the 4th and 5th dots are rarely used sledgehammers for specific situations but with Chimistry you're only really getting powers worth talking about at the 3rd level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:00:53-07:00","id":1514834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514825#post1514825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism is at least better than presence in this regard. Dog swarms are overwhelmingly strong if you can muster them. But therin lies the problem: it's hard to get a dog swarm in modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you have 6 dots, you can't controll a large number of animals.<br /> <br /> Animalism 1 requires Eye contact so that you can only communicate with one animal at a time, and realistically only out of combat.<br /> <br /> Animalism 2 lets you summon a pretty large number but doesn't give you any controll.<br /> <br /> To command multiple animals at a time you need Animalism 6 (Species Speech).<br /> <br /> I mean can summon the animals pre combat, give each commands one at a time and than hope for the best, but that's probably worse than just buying and training a bunch of Dogs the conventional way ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:08:55-07:00","id":1514835,"title":"","content":"No, you just need the second level. <br /> <br /> You can either <br /> <br /> A: Set commands with 1 that'll trigger when you use 2 or at certain signals, and then call them all and they'll get busy right away<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B: set one animal as a leader, and then just command the leader when you summon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:15:05-07:00","id":1514837,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>, while I do love the Ravnos' cultural thing built around acting as a divine punishment for other monsters who step out of line, the Wan Gui don't exist in VtM for me. The issue is that the 10,000 Demons then need to be something else and that, unless those 10,000 demons are Fey, their disciplines aren't much use. Sure animalism for hunting hounds (and such) and fortitude as unrelenting pursuers, but... eh. Sure, the Thallain are awful, but they've already got opposition, and I don't think the kindred are affected by their activities. Hunting infernalists, maybe, but I feel like the Assamites are happy to cover that, and the Sabbat already have their Inquisitors. <hr /><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514825#post1514825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimistry just isn't well designed. Even in V20 you've got terrible word choices like 'static' describing illusions but an example wine you can pick up and drink. That's in no way a static phantom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume &quot;static&quot; in this case means that it's like the difference between a png and a gif (except 3D). You can maybe move it around if it was made with Fata Morgana, but the image doesn't change. Light won't reflect off it, the shadows won't shift and such (so no &quot;sparkling chandeliers&quot;)<br /> <br /> I don't see an example of drinking wine, just &quot;A bucket of brackish water is as cool as chilled<i> champagne</i>, after all.\u200b&quot; The illusion is taste, not visual. A bucket off water masked with the illusory flavour of champagne doesn't have to have a static image overlaid, champagne can be clear. Maybe add carbonise it a bit beforehand, for authenticity.<br /> <br /> Horrid Reality fits the Changeling theme; you've just enchanted the target to see into the near dreaming, so the chimera within seem real to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":".  I am illiterate, apparently 06-13-2023, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:56:28-07:00","id":1514843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514835#post1514835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B: set one animal as a leader, and then just command the leader when you summon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said you need uniterupped eye contact for that, that will be hard to do in a fight.<br /> <br /> Animalism 1 also explicitly says that you can't force the animals to risk their lifes, which also limits it's use.<br /> <br /> And both things would require imo preparation and would likely work better if you use trained dogs (who could likely be trained to do the same with conventional means).<br /> <br /> It requires also a lot of successes to issue commands like this and to summon all the dogs. So you would likely need to max out Manipulation, Charisma, Animal Ken, Survival to pull that off somewhat reliably.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 06-13-2023, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T08:30:05-07:00","id":1514847,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Entertainment.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a clan whose unique discipline allows them to creates realistic illusions as detailed as they imagine them to be.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine how such thing would change even modern entertainment? Now put that across history.<br /> <br /> Bored cainites invite a ravnos ministrel to tell them a story with sounds and image. Now the tales of king arthur goes live in your courtroom!<br /> <br /> You can even uses that to be spicy. You're the prince of amsterdam and you hates the prince of rotterdam? Have your court ravnos creates an illusion of your rival to dance naked in the middle of elysium.<br /> <br /> <br /> Their potential as court jesters and entertainers is vast. They could also uses their power as scouts and messengers.<br /> <br /> Imagine, you're the prince of a place where someone or something is attacking mortals, fragilising the masquerade.<br /> <br /> You send a coterie to find the thing, with a ravnos with them, so that if they see the thing and fail to catch it, rather than trying to describe it, the ravnos can show you how it appeared.<br /> <br /> And then you can use your court ravnos to help protect the masquerade.<br /> <br /> Three men are found dead, mangled by one of your subjects in a frenzy? No problem, ask your ravnos to cast an illusion of a beast running across the city in view of people, ensuring they don't suspect that the killer is something unnatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can also use chimestry for defense. You want to ensure that no human hunters attempt to enter elysium? Ask your ravnos to creates the illusion of dozens of guards at every corner.<br /> <br /> <br /> The potential utility to vampire society is limitless. It's a shame that the ravnos are reduced to distrusted vagrantd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T09:18:01-07:00","id":1514850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514847#post1514847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bored cainites invite a ravnos ministrel to tell them a story with sounds and image. Now the tales of king arthur goes live in your courtroom!<br /> <br /> You can even uses that to be spicy. You're the prince of amsterdam and you hates the prince of rotterdam? Have your court ravnos creates an illusion of your rival to dance naked in the middle of elysium.<br /> <br /> Their potential as court jesters and entertainers is vast</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not that sure about <i>that</i> one<br /> <br /> Illusions created by Chimerstry can be seen for what they are by a victim who \u201cproves\u201d the illusion\u2019s falsehood (e.g., a person who walks up to an illusory wall, expresses his disbelief in it, and puts his hand through it effectively banishes the illusion), and explicitly incredible illusions are seen as false immediately (e.g., dragons breathing fire or gravity working in reverse).<br /> <br /> But of course, frequent targets of Chimerstry end up attempting to disbelieve everything around them, leading to derangements (and, quite often, to the amusement of the Ravnos).<br /> <br /> Most of the illusions lasts until the vampire leaves its vicinity (without \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Permanency) or until another person sees through it somehow.<br /> Without \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 Suspension of Disbelief the low level powers are risky to be used as entertainment...<br /> <br /> But I can see a Ravnos entertainer actually so good in his job, everyone thinks it <i>is an illuison</i>, while it is not, and when they see an illusion, they belive<i> it is talent</i>...<br /> <b>Gregorius Lakeritos</b>\u200b, the Wonder-Maker of Constantinople is a good example<br /> He was such a craftsman, his mechanical birds were true wonders - he discovered something in the Great Library of Alexandria that changed him profoundly, and caused the genesis of his work in clockwork automation<br /> While the Wonder-Maker mastered the first five level of Chimerstry (according his character sheet) his wonders were more of a mechanical kind, not illusions<br /> <br /> Following this, I can easly see the Ravnos as innovators and inventors - after all, before you would try warp reality, you first must understand reality, it laws and limits - so to speak &quot;be able to peek behind the magician's (creation?) courtain and understand what you see&quot;<br /> Thus mastering the unreal (Chimerstry) would work hand in hand with mastering the real (technology)<br /> I compared the wanderer Ravnos to the Silent Striders - Mesangers, couriers and guides<br /> But in this light they would be like the Glass Walkers - Bridge between Humanity, Technology - the ever changing world and advancements (in the other's older, more groudned mindend Cainites eyes &quot;miracles and wonders&quot;) and the &quot;old and static &quot;reality&quot;<br /> <br /> Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.<br /> Any Sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T09:19:44-07:00","id":1514851,"title":"","content":"This topic is cursed in my eyes, always ate my post....<br /> I will try again and will delete the original when appears<br /> Would be nice if the mods would do something about this tho'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514847#post1514847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-i