is work in clockwork automation<br /> While the Wonder-Maker mastered the first five level of Chimerstry (according his character sheet) his wonders were more of a mechanical kind, not illusions<br /> <br /> Following this, I can easly see the Ravnos as innovators and inventors - after all, before you would try warp reality, you first must understand reality, it laws and limits - so to speak &quot;be able to peek behind the magician's (creation?) courtain and understand what you see&quot;<br /> Thus mastering the unreal (Chimerstry) would work hand in hand with mastering the real (technology)<br /> I compared the wanderer Ravnos to the Silent Striders - Mesangers, couriers and guides<br /> But in this light they would be like the Glass Walkers - Bridge between Humanity, Technology - the ever changing world and advancements (in the other's older, more groudned mindend Cainites eyes &quot;miracles and wonders&quot;) and the &quot;old and static &quot;reality&quot;<br /> <br /> Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.<br /> Any Sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from technology.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T10:04:23-07:00","id":1514856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514185-what-service-could-the-ravnos-provide-larger-society?p=1514843#post1514843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said you need uniterupped eye contact for that, that will be hard to do in a fight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you prep all the local animals with Animalism commands. You can do that. You can do that long before any fight breaks out. Animalism 1 basically has Dominate 1 and 2 built into it, except there's no limit to the number of commands they can take (except maybe their memory and cognitive abilities) so you're actually really approaching Dominate 4 if you use it heavily enough. You know how an ordinary man can train a dog to give high fives? Yeah, you can do a lot more than that with feral whispers. Likely scenario: you prep all the dogs in your domain to fight whoever you point at or whoever's endangering you whenever you summon them. Completely legal. Yeah, you've gotta wait for them to get there, but once they're there, it's chow time with no extra imput needed from you. <br /> <br /> You can't force an animal to risk his life with this discipline alone, but you <i>can</i> get them to fight. You can expect them to run when things look bad, but given enough numbers animals will get pretty brave. How brave do ordinary animals need to be to target a crinos garou? let's not go there, but for vampires? Many are inclined to attack them anyway. Let's not forget many animals are likely to attack a vampire just because they don't have animal ken or animalism. <br /> <br /> However, If you <b>blood bond</b> the animals, you absolutely<i> can</i> expect them to fight to the death for your sake. A three point blood bond will have most creatures value you above their own lives. Crinos Garou? It's go time. remember, only a single drop of blood is needed to form blood bonds, so if your concept involves a wealthy country manor with 200 hunting dogs, by all means kill everything that comes to you. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this is far more the domain of' Tzmisce/Gangrel: the Ravnos are really too nomadic to accumulate like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:24:23-07:00","id":1514936,"title":"","content":"Problem is imo still, that it requires a lot of time and potentially resources to set up and to keep up, since if you are really going to fight something super natural, there is good chance that some dogs will die.<br /> <br /> Depending on what you are fighting, the dogs not dealing Agg damage might also be a problem.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem is imo that combats in VtM tends to be relatively short and deadly, even if the dog enter the fight one or two rounds after you summoned them, there is good chance that you are already dead at that point when you opponent has some some more direct combat powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}